TA-service
====

Collects systemd service health: total/active/failed unit counts and the list of failed units (with substate) via systemctl. Emits JSON events to index=main (sourcetype service:status) every 60s and service.* metrics to index=metrics (sourcetype service:metrics) - total, active, failed counts - with alarm status when any unit is in a failed state, plus dashboards.

Prerequisites
-------------
  * systemd (the Splunk host must run systemd) - no extra packages
  * Splunk Enterprise or Universal Forwarder 9.x - 10.6 (forwarder recommended
    on monitored hosts).
  * A metrics-typed index (default name: metrics) on the indexer:

      [metrics]
      datatype = metric

    Forwarders only need that index to exist on the indexer side.
  * No network egress, no root requirement beyond the Splunk service account.
    Fully standalone add-on with no dependencies.

Install
-------
Install on each monitored host (Apps > Install app from file, splunk install
app, or deployment server), restart Splunk, then verify:

  index=main sourcetype="service:status" | head

Search quick reference
----------------------
  index=main sourcetype="service:status" | head
  | mcatalog values(metric_name) where index=metrics metric_name="service.*" by host
  | mstats avg("service.*") where index=metrics span=60s by host

Usage
-----
Events: index=main sourcetype=service:status  (counts + failed unit names/substates)
Metrics: service.total / service.active / service.failed on index=metrics
Alarm status when >0 failed units.
Dashboards: TA-Service > Service Overview / Service Metrics

Configure
---------
Override the interval or destination index in etc/apps/TA-service/local/inputs.conf
(never edit default/).

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * Requires the Splunk service to be able to call systemctl (default as root).
  * Timer/socket/scope types are excluded; only service units are counted.

